Pin the OTA provider's secured port so the firewall can allow it.

python-matter-server launches chip-ota-provider-app with
`--secured-device-port 0`, which binds a random UDP port. During an update the
target node opens a new session to that port (QueryImage, then the BDX
transfer), so a host firewall that only allowlists ports drops it and the node
falls back from Querying to Idle ("Target node did not process the update
file"). The upstream Docker image runs without a host firewall, so it never
hits this. Keep the port in sync with otaProviderPort in
modules/services/matter-server.nix.

--- a/matter_server/server/ota/provider.py
+++ b/matter_server/server/ota/provider.py
@@ -178,7 +178,7 @@
             "--discriminator",
             str(ota_provider_discriminator),
             "--secured-device-port",
-            "0",
+            "5541",
             "--KVS",
             str(self._ota_provider_dir / f"chip_kvs_ota_provider_{timestamp}"),
             "--filepath",
